# SYNOPSIS

```usage
drive script
```

# DESCRIPTION

`drive` reads <script>, a step a line, and does what it says as a user's hands would, then says what the desktop did.
The pointer goes to mouse(4)'s `mousein` as absolute records (`A x y buttons`), and keys to kbdfs(4)'s `kbin` as HID usages, where the pointer's and keyboard's drivers write theirs: Radharc (radharc(4)) and the programs above it can't tell the difference.
It needs `/svc/mouse`, `/svc/kbdfs` and `/svc/windows` in its namespace, as a cpu(8) session has them where the image has a desktop, and `/svc/launcher` for `coldstart`.
`keydraw` and `coldstart` read Radharc's own clocks, as boot-rio's rio-test does, so the desktop's budgets can be judged where QEMU can't run them: `docs/boards/orangepi-6-plus/desktop-budgets.drive` is the Orange Pi 6 Plus's.

The steps, a line each; a blank line, or one whose first word starts with `#`, is none:

: `move` <x> <y>
  The pointer to (<x>, <y>), in the screen's pixels, the buttons as held.
: `press` [<button>], `release` [<button>]
  A button (`left`, `middle` or `right`; `left` if none) pressed or released where the pointer is.
: `click` [<button>] [<x> <y>], `rightclick` [<x> <y>]
  A move there if a place is given, 30 ms, the button pressed, 60 ms, and released.
: `key` <name> ...
  Each key pressed and released, 30 ms apart: a letter or digit, `f1` to `f12`, or `enter`, `esc`, `backspace`, `tab`, `space`, `up`, `down`, `left`, `right`, `home`, `end`, `pageup`, `pagedown`, `delete`, `ctrl`, `shift`, `alt` or `super`.
  Keys joined by `+` are a chord (`ctrl+w`): pressed in order, held 30 ms, and released in reverse.
: `type` <text>
  Each character typed, with shift where a US keyboard needs it: letters, digits, space and `-._/,`.
: `wait` <ms>
  A pause.
: `settle` [<quiet ms> [<limit ms>]]
  Waits for the input's first frame, up to two seconds, then until Radharc composes no frame for <quiet> ms (300 by default), at most <limit> ms after the last input (10000), then prints `drive: <line>: <ms> ms to the first frame, <ms> ms to the last, <n> frames;` and the processes that used CPU since the last `settle`, the most first, four at most (`cpu tracker 412 ms, windows 30 ms`), or `no CPU`.
  The times run from the first input since the last measure (a key's press, not its release; Radharc's frame count read just before it, and watched through the steps' own pauses) to the first frame composed after it, and to the last: the first is how long the desktop took to answer; the last includes any other window's frames in the meantime (a console's line, a clock), so it is an upper bound.
  `, not settled in <limit> ms` follows the frames if frames were still coming.
: `waitfor` <title> [<limit ms>]
  Waits until a window with that title is in Radharc's `list`, at most <limit> ms (10000), and prints the time from the first input since the last measure, or `not in <limit> ms`.
: `waitgone` <title> [<limit ms>]
  Waits until no window with that title is in Radharc's `list`, as `waitfor` does, or prints `still there after <limit> ms`.
: `mark` <text>
  Prints `drive: <text>`.
: `keydraw` <count> [<theme>]
  Types <count> keys into the focused window, `x` and Backspace in turn, so its text ends as it began, and reads Radharc's own timing of each from its `status` (`key draw`: from the key's arrival until the window presented, and the frames until that was on the screen), waiting up to five seconds for each.
  Prints how many were timed, their median and most, and three budget lines, `drive: budget name=terminal.key_draw.<theme> value=<ns> unit=ns limit=1000000`, `terminal.key_draw_max` and `terminal.key_glass` (the most frames, `limit=2`), named as boot-rio names them, with `.<theme>`: the one given, else the one Radharc's `status` says is in force.
: `coldstart` <app> [<theme>]
  Asks the launcher to start <app> (`start <app>` written to `/svc/launcher/ctl`) and waits up to ten seconds for Radharc's `first frame at` to name it; prints the time from the request to that frame and `drive: budget name=desktop.cold_start.<theme> value=<ns> unit=ns limit=50000000`, the theme as for `keydraw`.
  An app's first frame is shown only once a run: start it again after it has quit.
: `modeswitch` <count>
  Presses Super-Shift-T, chords(4)'s switch of the shown workspace between tile and space, <count> times, each half a second after Radharc has timed the last (its status's `switch <n> frames`), so an even count leaves the mode as it was; prints the frames each switch took to be on the glass and `drive: budget name=desktop.mode_switch value=<frames> unit=frames limit=2`, the most of them.
  The board's desktop image has an app, `twenty`, that holds twenty windows open for it (`echo start twenty >/svc/launcher/ctl`, and `kill twenty` to end it), as boot-workspaces times the switch with twenty.

At the end it prints `drive: done, <n> steps in <ms> ms`.

# EXAMPLES

From the dev machine, the desktop's menu opened and closed on a board running the desktop image, with the script in the current directory:

```text
$ cat menu.drive
move 1400 800
rightclick
settle
key esc
settle
$ vx cpu -r . -c 'drive /mnt/term/root/menu.drive' 192.168.0.19
```

